 ## Background
-The method originates from community-driven voxel shader implementations, specifically the "Voxel-World-Shader" by razzle-reinizu [S1, unofficial] and "Ray-Marched Voxel Simulation" by Joris Rijsdijk [S2, unofficial]. It is used in indie voxel games and educational graphics projects [S1, S2, unofficial].
+The method is documented in community shader repositories and graphics programming blog posts detailing ray-marched voxel rendering techniques [S1, S2, unofficial]. It is applied in indie voxel games and educational graphics projects to achieve real-time lighting on discrete voxel geometry [S1, S2, unofficial].
 
